    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0557" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg475"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1496.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <p>In further reply to the memorandum of the Embassy of Mexico, of the 8th ultimo,
                    in regard to the molestation of a Mexican courier <pb facs="0558" n="476"
                        xml:id="pg476"/> while carrying funds for Gen. Luque from Marfa to Presidio,
                    the Department of State has the honor to inclose for the embassy’s information a
                    copy of the letter from the governor of Texas,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d687-f1"/>
                    stating that he has sent to the sheriff of Presidio County copies of the
                    correspondence in relation to the matter, and instructions to give protection to
                    the agents of the Mexican Government.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-05"><hi rendition="#italic">May 5,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
